# Frontend Conventions

Framework-agnostic rules. Component syntax and state live in the framework files: Next.js uses `CLAUDE-FRONTEND-REACT.md` + `CLAUDE-FRONTEND-NEXT.md`; Vite (React SPA with TanStack Router) uses REACT + `CLAUDE-FRONTEND-VITE.md`; Nuxt 4 uses `CLAUDE-FRONTEND-VUE.md` + `CLAUDE-FRONTEND-NUXT.md`.

## Stack

- TypeScript in strict mode, no `any` (use `unknown` and narrow).
- SCSS Modules plus CSS custom properties for all styling (see `CLAUDE-STYLING.md`). No Tailwind.
- A server-state cache (TanStack Query) for all server state. No hand-rolled fetch-in-effect.

## Directories

`src/` (`app/` under Nuxt): `components/` (one folder per component: `Header/Header.tsx` + `Header.module.scss`), `features/` (one folder per feature slice), `api/` (own-backend fetch wrappers), `clients/` (third-party SDK wrappers), `services/` (domain logic), `state/` (stores and providers; `composables/` and `stores/` under Vue), `config/` (`queryClient.ts`, env parsing), `constants/`, `data/`, `styles/` (tokens, partials), `types/`.

- Create a directory only when it has contents.
- Never `lib/`, `utils/`, `helpers/` or other catch-alls; classify into one of the folders above.
- No `index.ts` barrel files; import from the file.

## Naming and imports

- SCSS modules: `PascalCase.module.scss`. Services, api and config modules: `camelCase.ts` named for what they do (`fetchTrips.ts`, `queryClient.ts`). Types: `camelCase.ts`.
- Import groups separated by blank lines: framework, third-party, local `@/` alias, relative siblings, styles last. Sort specifiers alphabetically.
- `import type` for type-only imports. Use `@/` for the source root; never `../../` beyond one level.
- Interfaces for component props (declared above the component in the same file); types for unions and utilities. Zod-inferred types when shared with the backend. Shared types go in `types/`.
- Prettier: single quotes, semicolons, trailing commas `all`, 4 spaces, 100 columns, `arrowParens: "always"`.
- ESLint: camelCase functions and variables, PascalCase types and components, `curly: 'error'` (always braces), no unused imports, no explicit `any`.

## API calls

- `api/apiFetch.ts` is the single typed transport (base URL from the framework's env var, `credentials: 'include'`, `X-Requested-With: XMLHttpRequest` for CSRF, throws with the server's error message). One exported function per backend route in its own module (`api/fetchTrips.ts`).
- Components never read env vars or call `api/` functions inside effects. They use the cache's query and mutation hooks. Cache client config lives in `config/queryClient.ts`.

## Error handling

- API and server errors go to a toast component, via the cache's `onError`. Never show raw error text or stack traces inline.
- Inline errors only for field-level form validation.

## E2E tests (Playwright)

- Tests live in `e2e/` at the repo root, one spec file per `## Section` of `docs/USER_STORIES.md` (mirror the file; do not invent groupings), plus 2 to 3 journey specs in `e2e/journeys/` (happy path, returning user, documented failure path).
- Exactly one test per documented user story, named with its ID: `test('US-1: home page discovery', ...)`. Journeys use only documented stories; add the story to the file first.
- Error paths live inside their story's test, not in an `error-states.spec.ts`.
- Mock external APIs (LLMs, search, payments) in E2E; real-API calls belong in a separate nightly smoke suite.
- Tag a fast lane (smoke, auth, one happy-path journey) with `@fast` in the test name.
- Assert data and behavior the user sees, never element presence alone.
- `fullyParallel: true`; isolate users and data instead of using `workers: 1`. Configure `projects` for chromium, webkit and mobile-safari.
- Fixtures (external API mocks, seeded users) in `e2e/fixtures/`; page objects and auth helpers in `e2e/helpers/`.
- Locally run `npx playwright test --only-changed=origin/main`; CI runs the full suite.
